From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:02:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: restart WLAN and Bluetooth after a CP2 reset

After a firmware assert or a missed loopcheck ack, the CP2 reset powers
WLAN and Bluetooth down and nothing powers them up again; both stay dead
until reboot. The "ready" notification that should follow the reset is
commented out.

Send it. WLAN probes its device again, which powers the chip up and
loads the firmware. Bluetooth powers its core up again if it was on,
sends PSKEY/RF again and then reports an HCI Hardware Error event, so
the host stack resets the controller. The vendor event sent so far
(ff 02 57 a5) is meant for the Android Bluetooth HAL; BlueZ ignores it.

Also remove the Bluetooth reset notifier when the driver goes away.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
